t that apply to saying you  can't come in unless you got a  vaccination  i think when you have something that is  a  personal right like smoking or like at  this point not getting a vaccination  you also have to say okay how does that  personal right  impact other people and what do i choose  for my business  one of the great things about business  in america is we are not government we  are free enterprise  and we have the right to make the kind  of choices we think are right for the  people who work for us  and the people who dine with us and  americas are free  and americans do not have to dine in  restaurants that  that don't welcome vaccine  non-vaccinated people if they choose not  to danny  i'm sorry go ahead so the small guy in  louisiana who's got you know a staff of  five  and a budget not anywhere as big as  yours he might look at this and go  yeah sounds great you're in new york  city but that's going to kill my  business  what do you say to him then he won't do  it yeah danny more than a hundred and  ten thousand restaurants  closed last year in the pandemic how's  the industry doing now  well you raised such an important point  because what i haven't shared this  morning  is that our industry was on its knees  for the last year and a half  in my business we laid off 95 percent of  our staff  at the end of march of last year i don't  want to go back and i know what will  happen  if we do not make our own restaurants  safe and the rates start to tick up  yeah that's when government's going to  step in including they're going to  impose the closures the capacity limits  we do not want to go back to that and  that's why this is so important as well  i hope other business leaders are  listening to you danny i'm very biased  about this particular topic because it's  scary  you have the vaccine and it it affects  other people if you don't want to get  vaccinated fine but now you're affecting  other people  that matters thanks for being here very  much thank

